{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 14, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 1, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0
    ,
      "why": "iterative is the shared-datapath family: one adder/shift stage reused, so it is the area floor for any given accuracy. It is the only family that can plausibly beat the area objective while still hitting >=1 MSPS at a modest Fmax. Accuracy needs max_abs_err <= 2^-10, which is met by W~14-16 with N~12-14; I keep W in 12-18 and N in 10-14 to let the optimizer find the cheapest (W,N) that clears the error bar, with small guards to avoid over-designing the angle/frac paths."
    },
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 14, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 1, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "k", "low": 2, "high": 4, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0,
      "why": "unrolled_k duplicates the datapath k times to raise throughput per cycle. It is the fallback if iterative's Fmax is too low to reach 1 MSPS (iterative does 1 result per N+3 cycles, so it needs Fmax >= (N+3) MHz). k=2..4 gives 2-4x throughput at the cost of kx datapath area; I keep k small (2-4) because area is the primary objective, so only the minimum k that clears the throughput constraint should win. Same accuracy ranges as iterative since the bits are identical."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "No fleet facts yet, so I seed both of my assigned families. The spec is area-dominated with a hard throughput floor (>=1 MSPS) and a hard accuracy floor (max_abs_err <= 2^-10). Accuracy is width/iteration driven and identical across families, so I pin a tight accuracy box (W 12-18, N 10-14, small guards, both roundings) that comfortably clears 2^-10 without wasting budget on over-accurate corners. The real trade-off is area vs throughput: iterative is the area floor but does 1 result per N+3 cycles, so it needs a high Fmax to hit 1 MSPS; unrolled_k trades duplicated-datapath area for kx throughput. I give iterative the larger share because it is the most likely area winner, and unrolled_k the remainder to map the throughput-vs-area knee in case iterative's Fmax falls short of the throughput constraint. Both families share the same accuracy ranges so the merged front is directly comparable on area/accuracy."
}

